Multi-subscriptions in the SAPL binary format, as the RSocket API receives them on a connection
with the data MIME type application/vnd.sapl.binary.

A payload is the lead byte 00, the text region and the structure: the number of entries, then per entry the id as a
length that names the next bytes of the region, and the subscription as in
subscriptions-binary.cases. An id is neither empty nor blank, and no id occurs twice. At most 256
entries are allowed; a larger number refuses the payload before any entry is read.

The document is the payload in hexadecimal bytes. A '//' starts a comment to the end of the line.
The expectation is either the ids in their order, as a JSON array, or 'refused' with the reason.

=== two subscriptions
00 0c 61 61 6c 69 63 65 62 61 6c 69 63 65   // region "aalicebalice"
02                                        // two entries
01 25 00 00 00 60                         // "a": subject "alice"
01 25 00 00 00 60                         // "b": subject "alice"
---
ids: ["a","b"]

=== no entries
00 00 00
---
ids: []

=== an empty id
00 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 60
---
refused: blank id

=== an id of a space
00 01 20 01 01 00 00 00 00 60
---
refused: blank id

=== an id given twice
00 02 61 61 02 01 00 00 00 00 60 01 00 00 00 00 60
---
refused: duplicate id

=== an entry whose subscription is malformed
00 01 61 01 01 0b 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== an entry that is cut off
00 01 61 01 01 00 00
---
refused: malformed

=== fewer entries than announced
00 01 61 02 01 00 00 00 00 60
---
refused: malformed

=== a byte after the last entry
00 01 61 01 01 00 00 00 00 60 00
---
refused: malformed

=== 257 entries announced, refused before any is read
00 00 81 02
---
refused: too many subscriptions
